### Phase 5: calling secured services with a real token.
### Get one with:  ./infrastructure/keycloak/pkce-login.sh alice 2>/dev/null
### (access tokens live 5 minutes; get a fresh one when you see 401)

@user = http://localhost:8081
@account = http://localhost:8082
@token = paste-access-token-here

### Who does user-service think I am?
GET {{user}}/api/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token: 401 problem+json and "WWW-Authenticate: Bearer"
GET {{user}}/api/customers

### Garbage token: 401 with error="invalid_token"
GET {{user}}/api/customers
Authorization: Bearer not-a-jwt

### With a token
GET {{account}}/api/accounts?ownerId=7f3c9a2e-1b4d-4e8a-9c6f-2d5b8e1a0f3c
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Open an account (still any authenticated user; roles arrive in Phase 8)
POST {{account}}/api/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ownerId": "7f3c9a2e-1b4d-4e8a-9c6f-2d5b8e1a0f3c", "type": "SAVINGS", "currency": "THB" }

### Health: public summary; details only with an ADMIN (ada) token
GET {{account}}/actuator/health
